  PUY4XnyZV: {
    defaultValue:
      '<h4 dir="auto">A strategic repositioning and identity refresh created to sharpen the brand’s presence, clarify its message, and build a&nbsp;more distinctive digital&nbsp;experience.</h4><h4 dir="auto"><br class="trailing-break"></h4><h6 dir="auto">Overview</h6><p dir="auto">Heatwave needed a campaign language that could match its pace and attitude without falling into visual chaos. The goal was to create a system that feels immediate, bold, and easy to recognize, while still leaving enough flexibility for different drops, announcements, and supporting content.</p><p dir="auto"><br class="trailing-break"></p><h6 dir="auto">Challenge</h6><p dir="auto">The brand already had energy, but its campaign materials lacked consistency and a clear visual hierarchy. Some assets felt too loud, others too generic, and together they did not create a strong or unified impression. The challenge was to bring more discipline to the rollout without losing the raw intensity that made the brand interesting in the first place.</p><p dir="auto"><br class="trailing-break"></p><h6 dir="auto">Our Approach</h6><p dir="auto">We built the campaign around scale, contrast, and repetition. Large typographic statements, tighter layout rules, and a more deliberate use of graphic tension helped shape a system that could carry across hero assets, social content, posters, and launch materials. Instead of adding more elements, we focused on making a smaller set of decisions work harder and feel more intentional.</p><p dir="auto"><br class="trailing-break"></p><h6 dir="auto">Outcome</h6><p dir="auto">The new campaign system gave Heatwave a stronger visual rhythm and a much more recognizable launch presence across 21 final assets delivered in 4 weeks. The result was a sharper and more cohesive rollout that improved consistency, increased flexibility for future drops, and gave the brand a clearer visual impact across every major touchpoint.</p><p dir="auto"><br class="trailing-break"></p><p dir="auto"><strong>Iris Coleman</strong> (Campaign Direction)</p><p dir="auto"><strong>Felix Hart</strong> (Art Direction)</p><p dir="auto"><strong>Naomi Blake</strong> (Copywriting)</p>',
    title: "Project Info",
    type: ControlType.RichText,
  },
